    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3165" root="بلد" body-key="b">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بيض</span></b> .] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <i>A trace, mark,</i> or <i>vestige,</i> (T, S, M, K,
[in the K mentioned in two places, but in the
latter of these omitted in the CK,]) of a house,
or dwelling: (TA:) and <i>a mark remaining upon
the body:</i> (A'Obeyd, T:) pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَبْلَادٌ</span>. (S, A'Obeyd,
M, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  The <i>origin,</i> or <i>an element,</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُنْصُر</span>,)
of a thing. (Th, M, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  See also the next
paragraph, in three places: ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b5-  and see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بُلْدَةٌ</span>.

